  "answer": "Project Zenith is a multi-phase initiative with varying descriptions across different communications. Initially introduced in June 2023 (content:03) and July 2023 (content:04) with a focus on data analytics and cloud storage optimization respectively, the project has seen significant developments. A budget of $2 million was approved (content:08), with an initial phase one budget of $500,000 (content:03). Key milestones include the approval of a $15,000 training budget (content:10), the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype (content:05), and a breakthrough in predictive analytics (content:01). The project involves various team members including Sarah Tan, Marcus Cole, Tom, and Neil. Updates indicate a focus on efficiency gains, security protocol enhancements (including multi-factor authentication effective January next year), and user experience improvements. Feedback was sought by the end of November, and detailed reports were scheduled for staff meetings in August and November."
